=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE class RakuAST::Name::Part::Simple

=SUBTITLE Represent a string part of a Name

    class RakuAST::Name::Part::Simple { }

The C<RakuAST::Name::Part::Simple> class represents a simple string
part of a L<C<RakuAST::Name>|/type/RakuAST/Name> object.

=head2 Object introspection

C<RakuAST::Name::Part::Simple> object is typically created when parsing
Raku Programming Language code.  So most developers will only need to
know how to introspect the objects created.

=head3 name

=begin code :preamble<my $part>
say $part.name;  # foo
=end code

Returns the name of this part as a C<Str>.

=head3 is-empty

=begin code :preamble<my $part>
say $part.is-empty;  # True or False
=end code

Returns whether this is an empty part of a C<RakuAST::Name>.

=head3 is-pseudo-package

=begin code :preamble<my $part>
say $part.is-pseudo-package;  # True or False
=end code

Returns whether this part could be considered a pseudo-package name.
The following names would be considered pseudo-packages:

=item CALLER
=item CALLERS
=item CLIENT
=item COMPILING
=item CORE
=item DYNAMIC
=item LEXICAL
=item MY
=item OUR
=item OUTER
=item OUTERS
=item SETTING
=item UNIT

=head2 Object creation

=begin code :preamble<my $name>
my $part = RakuAST::Name::Part::Simple.new($name);
=end code

A C<RakuAST::Name::Part::Simple> object is instantiated with the C<.new>
method.  It takes a single argument: the string to be used for the name.

=end pod
